-->

	<modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
	<groupId>org.smartblackbox</groupId>
	<artifactId>QuantumFieldSimulator</artifactId>
	<version>0.1</version>
	<name>Duy Quoc Nguyen</name>
	<description>
		This application simulates the quantum field theory.
		Inititially it was developed to simulate the double slit experiment.
		It uses a simple motion formula to simulate the light wave.
		By defining the slits in the simulator, the interference patterns can be
		simulated.
		Even walls/mirrors can be defined freely in 3D quantum field.
		There are also other files to simulate, for example rain drops or
		detecting the speed of light.
		This simulator does not approximate the real world values,
		but rather simulates the properties of the light wave due to a lack of
		CPU/GPU power.
	</description>

